{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgCpF4sB4fwBdqd25xf2h","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The framework component is `ActionMenuButton2` in `openmrs-esm-core`. Five components in the patient chart app render it, and one test file mocks it. All five chart usages are confirmed by reading the files. The chart's `routes.json` files, which register the windows these buttons open, were not checked.\n\n**Changed declaration:** `ActionMenuButton2` at `openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-styleguide/src/workspaces2/action-menu2/action-menu-button2.component.tsx:66-143`, with props in `ActionMenuButtonProps2` at lines 31-50. Its click behaviour (lines 86-100) is: hide or restore the window if it is open, otherwise run `onBeforeWorkspaceLaunch` and then `launchWorkspace2`. The window it controls is found by matching `extension.extensionId` against open window names (line 77).\n\n**Confirmed affected in the patient chart app:**\n\n1. `openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-orders-app/src/order-basket-action-button/order-basket-action-button.component.tsx:13-33`. Uses `tagContent` (order count), `workspaceToLaunch` with `windowProps`, and `onBeforeWorkspaceLaunch`. Most exposed: it depends on the badge, the window-visibility toggle and the pre-launch hook.\n2. `openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-notes-app/src/visit-note-action-button.extension.tsx:10-26`. Uses `workspaceToLaunch` and `onBeforeWorkspaceLaunch={startVisitIfNeeded}`, so it depends on the visit-start gate.\n3. `openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-forms-app/src/clinical-form-action-button.component.tsx:10-27`. Same pattern as the visit-note button: `workspaceToLaunch` and `onBeforeWorkspaceLaunch`.\n4. `openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-lists-app/src/action-button/patient-lists-action-button.extension.tsx:5-17`. Uses `icon`, `label` and `workspaceToLaunch` only, so it is exposed to changes in the window toggle and launch logic.\n5. `openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-task-list-app/src/launch-button/task-list-launch-button.extension.tsx:5-18`. Uses `icon`, `label` and `workspaceToLaunch` only.\n\n**Likely affected, not verified:**\n\n6. `openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-forms-app/src/clinical-form-action-button.test.tsx:8-15` and `:26-49`. Mocks `ActionMenuButton2` with a function that reads `label` and `tagContent`. Tests break if those prop names change. The test also asserts on the rendered label text.\n7. Test mocks in `openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-framework/mock.tsx:119` and `mock-jest.tsx:118`. These mock the component for every consumer's tests and destructure `label`, `tagContent` and `icon`, so they need updating with any prop change. These are in the core repo, not the chart app.\n\n**Outside the chart app (same framework component, for completeness):**\n`openmrs-esm-patient-management` also uses it in `packages/esm-ward-app/src/action-menu-buttons/` (order-basket, transfer, discharge, clinical-forms), `ward-workspace/ward-patient-notes/notes-action-button.component.tsx`, `ward-workspace/patient-details/ward-patient-action-button.component.tsx`. The o3 docs (`openmrs-contrib-o3-docs`, `content/en-US/docs/workspaces/siderail-and-bottom-nav.mdx` and `migrate-to-workspace-v2.mdx`) describe the component's contract and are also affected in their wording if behaviour changes.\n\n**Not checked:**\n- The `routes.json` files in the chart app that register the `workspaceWindows2` entries and extension IDs. A change to how the extension ID is matched to the window name would affect all five buttons through these registrations.\n- Dynamic or indirect use (for example, extension lookup by string name).\n- Any other repos beyond the grep results above.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-styleguide/src/workspaces2/action-menu2/action-menu-button2.component.tsx\", \"startLine\": 66, \"endLine\"